UNIX-TOOLBOX

unix-toolbox is a small collection of self-contained Unix helper tools
and scripts used in tmux, minimal window managers, and traditional
Slackware- and BSD-style workflows.


TOOLS

The repository currently includes:

- sbmk
  Helper script for SlackBuild maintenance tasks.

- mk-slackbuild
  Generates a conservative SlackBuild skeleton intended to be edited
  by hand.

- scratch
  Disposable nvi-based scratchpad for temporary text staging.

- slackfetch
  Small system information script focused on Slackware Linux.

- t
  Minimal editor-centric todo.txt manager using plain text files.

- tmux-status
  Minimal system status script for use in the tmux status bar.


OVERVIEW

Each tool lives in its own directory and is documented locally.

The tools are intentionally small and independent, with no shared
framework, build system, or runtime dependency.


DESIGN

unix-toolbox follows a conservative Unix-style design:

- one tool per directory
- simple and readable implementations
- no daemons or background services
- no mandatory configuration files
- suitable for minimal and traditional systems


INSTALLATION

There is no global installation procedure.

Individual tools can be installed by copying them into a directory
listed in PATH, for example:

  install -m 0755 toolname ~/.local/bin/toolname

Refer to each tool’s README for usage details.


